    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49445" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turbĭdo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		turbidus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to trouble</i>, <i>to make
			turbid</i>, <i>to disturb</i>, <i>obscure</i> (post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aquam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 49 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aër turbidatus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 2, § 165</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laetitiam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 1, § 67</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">serenitatem animae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 6, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
